Z||000000||maryjane||06-10-2001||01:56 PM||||This question was fwd'd to me from a friend w/o internet access. (1992 Bonneville/3.9 eng/supercharged.) The supercharger has stopped working, I assume locked up. His intentions are to remove the belt,reroute the ducting and run without the supercharger.<BR>My gut feeling is that is not a good idea but I'm not familar with gasoline engs with turbos or superchargers. Diesels doo not run worth a d*** without the turbo installed because of comp ratio differences,timing, and different valves and injectors used in turbo'd engines.What are his options? If he can do it what is needed. What are the dangers to be encountered? I don't know the level of his mechanical ability,(not sure of mine sometimes),so be kind. If someone wants to move this to the tech section,ok,I know it is not Fiero related. Thanks in advance.<BR>Don<p>[This message has been edited by maryjane (edited 06-10-2001).]||||reg||5
Z||000001||maryjane||06-10-2001||06:07 PM||||bump-anybody?||||reg||1
Z||000002||Formula88||06-11-2001||09:08 AM||||It should run ok, but not great.  The 3800 is a good engine without the SC, but the SC is going to be a big blockage to airflow now.  Give it a try.  It shouldn't hurt anything, but it may not run well enough to be very useful.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Formula||06-11-2001||09:48 AM||||it probably wont run good because the lower the compression of the engine when they build it to be supercharged.  it might not be that bad though<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sigformulagt.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||KnightRyder31||06-11-2001||04:40 PM||||Ummm...<BR>be sure to tell your friend that the engine that you referred to as the "3.9" is in fact a 3.8, or 3800.||||reg||1
Z||000005||maryjane||06-12-2001||01:54 AM||||Thanks for the replys. I'll pass them along.<BR>Don||||reg||14
Z||000006||terryk||06-12-2001||03:31 PM||||The clearance through the blower is so tight that if you take the belt off, the blower will spin when you rev engine. Therefore, with the blower locked up, it will restrict the air flow into the engine. <P>Obviously you will lose power and it might be even worse.<P>If he's got rotor-lock (rare but possible on an Eaton), it's not good. Usually, the nose drive starts to rattle bad and is annoying enough to make you want to fix it.<P>TK||||reg||1
